# P1a / STEP 2a — LF everywhere for text, binaries declared.
#
# Why: the CSP pins sha256 over the EXACT bytes of the inline boot script in
# index.html (pin-csp.mjs, seo-routes.mjs, server.ts). A checkout that flips
# LF→CRLF changes those bytes, so the pinned hash stops matching the shipped
# script and the browser blocks the boot (bug B1). With `eol=lf` the working
# copy is always LF, on every platform, so the hash is stable.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
